   "title": "How to Find HCF and LCM Using Prime Factorisation",
   "content": "<p>Write each number as a product of primes using a factor tree. Then:</p><p><strong>HCF:</strong> Multiply the primes that appear in <em>both</em> factorisations (use the lower power).</p><p><strong>LCM:</strong> Multiply all primes that appear in <em>either</em> factorisation (use the higher power).</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>Find HCF and LCM of 24 and 36</strong></p><p>\\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3\\), \\(36 = 2^2 \\times 3^2\\)</p><p><strong>HCF</strong> = \\(2^2 \\times 3 = 12\\)</p><p><strong>LCM</strong> = \\(2^3 \\times 3^2 = 72\\)</p>"
  },
